<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
  <h3 itemprop="name">Can I use my old Kindle's case and charger with a new model?</h3>
  <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
    <div itemprop="text">
      <p>It depends. Most recent Kindles (Paperwhite 12th Gen, Colorsoft, Scribe 2026) use USB-C, so your old Micro-USB cables will not fit. Cases are not cross-compatible between generations — you will need a case designed for your specific model. Chargers are interchangeable as long as they are USB-C.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
  <h3 itemprop="name">Will my audiobooks and Audible purchases transfer to a new Kindle?</h3>
  <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
    <div itemprop="text">
      <p>Yes. Audible audiobooks are tied to your Amazon account, not your device. Sign in on the new Kindle and your entire Audible library is available. The Kindle Scribe and Kindle Colorsoft support Bluetooth headphones for Audible playback.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
  <h3 itemprop="name">How do I transfer my Kindle library to a different brand of e-reader?</h3>
  <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
    <div itemprop="text">
      <p>If you are switching to Kobo, PocketBook, or another brand, you will need to download your books as EPUB files (DRM-free where available) and then transfer them via USB or Calibre. Many publishers now offer DRM-free EPUB downloads from Amazon. For DRM-protected books, check our <a href="/blog/migrate-kindle-library-to-epub/">guide to migrating your Kindle library to EPUB</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
  <h3 itemprop="name">What happens to my Kindle Unlimited books when I upgrade?</h3>
  <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
    <div itemprop="text">
      <p>Nothing changes. Kindle Unlimited is tied to your account. Sign in on the new Kindle, open the Kindle Unlimited section, and re-download any titles you are currently reading. Your borrowed books, reading position, and notes sync automatically via Whispersync.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

